two children, two dogs.

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:05.130
I do not need anymore in
my house, but it's hard.

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:06.270
They're so cute.

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:07.103
- I know.

00:01:07.103 --> 00:01:09.570
My 5-year-old son came with me here today.

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:12.577
And he just said to me,
mommy, I want Snowflake.

00:01:12.577 --> 00:01:14.100
[Audience] Ahhh
[Kelly Clarkson] Ahhh

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:14.933
That's hard to...

00:01:14.933 --> 00:01:17.550
- I think our 14-year-old dog at home

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.531
would have a heart attack and die

00:01:19.531 --> 00:01:20.823
if I brought home Snowflake.

00:01:20.823 --> 00:01:22.950
- That kind of energy is different.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:24.480
Because I brought home Charlie to Henry

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.760
and they're like four
years difference, I think.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:28.743
And Henry was not impressed.

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:31.860
I let my daughter get a dog

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.971
and Henry was like, what's happening here?

00:01:33.971 --> 00:01:34.804
- Oh no.

00:01:34.804 --> 00:01:35.910
- Yeah, they're fine now.

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:37.620
But do you get starstruck still

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:39.720
by authors like that you love?

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:44.720
- Yes, I cry every time I meet
someone that I really admire.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:46.433
I don't know.

00:01:46.433 --> 00:01:48.150
I have this reaction.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:49.410
Because it's so intense that I,

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:50.910
my body just goes to tears.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.850
- Yes, well, I think it's
when it's someone that

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:58.023
I have admired and whose
journey inspired my journey.

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:02.670
All of those emotions from like wishing

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:04.230
and hoping to like get to

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:05.580
that same point in my career.

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:06.413
- Inspiration.

00:02:06.413 --> 00:02:08.130
- It hits me at once.

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:09.600
And I'll, like, I'll never forget,

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.800
I was at this book convention

00:02:12.901 --> 00:02:15.540
and I was on a panel with
this author Tamara Pierce,

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.310
who I had like grown up reading.

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:18.873
I loved her books.

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:21.750
And I was on a panel with
her, like, as a peer,

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:23.670
like that, that shouldn't happen.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:26.070
Like, I am not smart or cool enough

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:27.300
to be sitting next to this woman.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.310
- I Have been in this situation musically.

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:30.600
And you're like, why am I here?

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:34.050
- And so I like walk in and
like sit down next to her

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:38.028
and I just, her name's
Tamara and I go, 'Hi Tammy.'

00:02:38.028 --> 00:02:39.510
- (gasping)

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:41.880
You're like besties off the bat

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:43.230
- I wanted to die.

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:45.780
And she just was like
very, she was so gracious.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:47.610
She was just like, oh,
hello. It's nice to meet you.

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:49.470
And then I just started telling her like,

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:52.650
I'm only here today because
of the work that you did,

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:54.758
because of the trail that you blazed.

00:02:54.758 --> 00:02:55.591
- I bet that made her feel good.

00:02:55.591 --> 00:02:57.750
- And I just, well, yes, but
I started sobbing like this.

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:00.086
And not like beautiful tears.

00:03:00.086 --> 00:03:01.740
- Not Rachel McAdams, no.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:03.780
- Mine were like (mimics crying)

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:06.840
And this was before a
panel was about to begin.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:10.200
So there was a room full of
people there witnessing this.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:13.680
Like absolute meltdown.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:16.050
And thankfully she was so kind

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:18.690
and at the end of my
whole like sobbing rant,

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:21.660
she was just like, it's
very nice to meet you.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:23.490
- You know what's interesting
though is you have now fans

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:24.690
that probably do that with you,

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:26.400
that you inspire and
you touch and they cry.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:27.390
And you're like, no, I get it.

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:28.380
I'm like this with other people.

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:29.213
- Oh yeah, I know.

00:03:29.213 --> 00:03:30.773
I'm like, I'm like, don't ever
be embarrassed by the tears.

00:03:30.773 --> 00:03:31.606
- [Kelly] Absolutely.

00:03:31.606 --> 00:03:32.439
- 'Cause I am that person.

00:03:32.439 --> 00:03:34.440
And the tears are a wonderful thing.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:35.273
Like it tells you

00:03:35.273 --> 00:03:36.106
that it means
- [Kelly] Means it impacts you

00:03:36.106 --> 00:03:36.939
- Something to you

00:03:36.939 --> 00:03:37.772
Exactly, exactly

00:03:37.772 --> 00:03:39.930
But then the, like, my
readers start crying

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:41.160
and then I start crying.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:43.320
- I'm a contagious crier as well.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:44.550
Someone cries on the couch and I'm like,

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:45.420
oh man, it's over.

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:46.253
- No, no..

00:03:46.253 --> 00:03:47.086
- And I'm just, it's done.

00:03:47.086 --> 00:03:48.414
The makeup's ruined for ever

00:03:48.414 --> 00:03:49.650
- It's like, I wanna cry all the time.

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:50.483
What's happening?

00:03:50.483 --> 00:03:52.204
I think it's called menopause, whatever.

00:03:52.204 --> 00:03:53.880
- (laughing)

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:55.830
- But you say like, explaining the book

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:57.270
is kind of hard, right?

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.320
The new book.

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:00.060
Why do you think it, what can you tell us?

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:01.440
- Yeah, so this is the third book

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:02.390
in my Crescent City series.

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:03.570
- So you don't wanna ruin anything.

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:04.650
- Yeah, so no spoilers.

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:06.033
My lips are sealed.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.120
But this series is kind of like a mashup

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:12.270
between like fantasy, paranormal romance,

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:13.290
little urban fantasy.

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:17.820
So it's a separate fantasy
world, but like a modern world.

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:19.320
So there are all these magical creatures

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:20.153
living in that world.

00:04:20.153 --> 00:04:21.132
- Love, I'm in.

00:04:21.132 --> 00:04:22.920
- And there's lots of like action

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:25.170
and a lot of like very steamy stuff.

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:26.494
- I'm in

00:04:26.494 --> 00:04:27.331
- Lots of hot dudes.

00:04:27.331 --> 00:04:28.530
- Alright.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:30.900
- And then like, it's kind
of like all my other books,

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:32.984
I've got a couple different series

00:04:32.984 --> 00:04:34.260
where they're all about like young women

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:38.730
finding their strength,
saving the day, kicking butt.

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:39.563
- Love it.

00:04:39.563 --> 00:04:41.610
- Yeah, so there's that,

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:42.810
that's a big part of it.

00:04:44.096 --> 00:04:45.330
- It must be hard to not be able to talk

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:46.163
about the book though

00:04:46.163 --> 00:04:46.996
'cause you're like,

00:04:46.996 --> 00:04:47.829
'Oh wait, fans might
not be caught up this.'

00:04:47.829 --> 00:04:48.662
- Yes, yes.

00:04:48.662 --> 00:04:50.250
- And book two ends on
a major cliffhanger,

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:52.560
so I can't even like
explain the beginning.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.590
Like just the general
premise of this third book.

00:04:55.590 --> 00:04:57.030
- Is that normal by the way?

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:58.140
Like last night, I mean,

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:00.060
even Vulture wrote
something about you, like,

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:02.340
you did this release and
like it just blew up.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:04.890
It literally was like Taylor
Swift was releasing an album,

00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:06.870
